# No inline imports

Put every import at the top of the file. Never import inside a function, method,
conditional, or loop.

```python
# ❌ BAD
def test_save_entry_creates_mesh_content(tmp_path, monkeypatch):
    from main.content_generation.save_entry import update_or_generate_from_request
    response = update_or_generate_from_request({...})

# ✅ GOOD
from main.content_generation.save_entry import update_or_generate_from_request

def test_save_entry_creates_mesh_content(tmp_path, monkeypatch):
    response = update_or_generate_from_request({...})
```

Do not use a mid-function import to avoid circular imports, missing optional
dependencies, or test collection side effects. Fix the module graph or import
at the top instead.
